  "notes": "West leads the ♠K against 6♦. The defense wins the first spade trick and continues spades. To maximize the chances of making the contract, South should ruff with the ♦Q or ♦J.\n\nSouth should cross to the ♥K and lead diamonds through East. Thanks to South's unblocking play at trick 2, the lead will remain in dummy to repeat the trump finesse. South will be able to pick up 3 trumps to the ♦K in East's hand.\n\nIf South had ruffed with the ♦2 at trick 2 and crossed to the ♥K to finesse diamonds, South would have had to risk a club ruff in the dummy in order to finesse diamonds again. If East was dealt a singleton club he would be able to overruff with the ♦K.",
  "commentary_paragraphs": [
    "West leads the ♠K against 6♦. The defense wins the first spade trick and continues spades. To maximize the chances of making the contract, South should ruff with the ♦Q or ♦J.",
    "South should cross to the ♥K and lead diamonds through East. Thanks to South's unblocking play at trick 2, the lead will remain in dummy to repeat the trump finesse. South will be able to pick up 3 trumps to the ♦K in East's hand.",
